# Test: ze support --reason embeds reason in manifest
# VALIDATES: AC-7 of spec-support.md -- reason metadata
# NOTE: the runner splits exec= on whitespace (no shell quoting), so the reason
# must be a single token; a multi-word "BGP flap test" would be parsed as extra
# args. The value is matched against the --json manifest, hence the quotes.
# The archive is written into the per-test working dir (--output .) which the
# runner allocates fresh and cleans up. Writing to the shared /tmp caused
# "file exists" collisions (archive names are only second-granular) and is
# forbidden by the project no-/tmp convention.
tmpfs=.support-out-keep:terminator=EOF_KEEP
placeholder so the runner allocates an isolated working dir
EOF_KEEP

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze support --module version --reason BGP-flap-test --json --output .
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="BGP-flap-test"
expect=stdout:contains="reason"
